A||||12||ChadMan||Guy in Navigator tried to kill me today!  (crazy but true)||||8||
Z||000000||ChadMan||06-08-2001||11:13 PM||||So there I was driving home from work on a beautiful sunny Friday afternoon in my Fiero - driving north on Riverside Drive, a four-lane road.  <P>I come to a red light (Fishinger, for you Columbusites) and I'm seven or eight cars back from the light in the right lane and I see the first car is a box van/moving truck.  The left lane is empty and I thought about going up there and taking "pole position," but decided against it because I wasn't in that big a hurry and the left lane ends about 1/8 mile past the intersection (important).<P>The light turns green and the line of traffic starts out slowly, nose to tail behind the box van, reaching about 35 mph.  As we approach the merge, I notice this white Navigator coming up the left lane at 55-60 mph.  I wonder to myself where he's going to go; the box van is past the merge and everyone is nose to tail behind it.<P>The Navigator draws up alongside me with his grille even with my door and nails his brakes, but the guy behind me glues himself to my rear end so Mr. SUV Yuppie Scumbag can't squeeze in.  <P>I can't speed up because there's a car right in front of me.  I can't slow down because there's a guy two feet off my back bumper.  We reach the merge and the Navigator is now over the double yellow in the oncoming lanes.  Southbound cars are swerving and honking to avoid him and STILL THE BASTARD WON'T SLOW DOWN.  Instead, he starts to drift right, thinking he will use his 6500-pound piece of camel crap to intimidate the guy behind me into slowing down.  Instead, that guy drifts right, but stays on the gas, and I don't have much choice but to drift right too.  <P>With two wheels on the berm and trees flying past on the right, I run out of room and stop drifting right.  The Navigator bumps me in the left-rear fender with his right-front fender.  The Navigator panics, cuts left toward an oncoming car, then brakes and cuts right.  The guy behind me nails the brakes and the Navigator slots in behind me.<P>To my amazement, I wasn't really scared and I wasn't really mad...just sort of dumbfounded.  I read his front tag number in my rearview and jotted it down, and I noticed the S.O.B. was yammering away on his cell phone.  He cut down a side street to run away and I drove into the heart of Upper Arlington, flagged down a police officer and told him the story.<P>Would you believe the phucker in the Navigator called the cops, reported it as a hit-skip and said I tried to pass him?  Luckily, the officer smelled a rat and said the guy seemed really nervous and reluctant to give his name, while I was forthcoming and cooperative (of course I was...I didn't have to lie!).  The Fiero is fine - just has a four-inch long white scuff above the left-rear fender which will buff out easily.<P>What's weird is, the cop didn't cite me, but he said they didn't cite the Navigator yuppie either (though he did use the word "yet").<P>What do you think will happen?  Should I pursue this myself and try and get some money from this bastard, or let it go?  Is there any chance of me getting cited (can't see how)?  I'm busy at work right now and am going on vacation in two weeks...hate to say it but I'd probably let it go if I can -- I don't have time to dance around the courts with this jagoff.<P>If you've read this far, thank you!||||reg||8
Z||000001||fierofrek||06-08-2001||11:55 PM||||I don't know, I think I would try to NAIL the Bas43rd for everything I could. If he/she did it once, he/she will do it again till they kill someone, or get busted.(sometimes being busted doesn't even work)<BR>Then again, you are going on Vac. and would hate to miss that! contact the police and get a report within 24 hours, then you have a little while before you can't do anything about it, like a month I think. <BR>just my $.02. good luck whatever you do, and have a good Vac!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||06-09-2001||12:55 AM||||Be sure to report it to you insurance co.  Tell them you do not want to make a claim, just an FYI in case the fool tries to track you down and make a claim.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||06-09-2001||01:31 AM||||Some guy in a tanker truck tried to kill me today...OK maybe not that dramatic, but I was in the right lane, he was about 2 or 3 carlengths behind in the right...left lane was ending, but it was a ways ahead. I see the merge sign and put my signal on...the trucker actually sped up so I couldn't fit in...merge getting closer, and the car in front of the trucker creeped ahead, so I slid in behind him. Trucker then decides to lay on his horn and get on my @ss. I gave him a piece of my mind in the form of my middle finger... Why do people actually *attempt* to be jack@sses on the road? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||06-09-2001||03:27 AM||||I would DEFINATELY pursue this.  Get a settlement!  Make him pay for your repairs, no matter how minor.  He shouldn't get away with it just because it was no where near as bad as it could have been.  Also, I  don't see how you could be cited.  Give 'em hell!<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000005||Uaana||06-09-2001||03:39 AM||||I know what you mean I deal with a similar set up daily on my way to work. 3 lanes drop to 2 in a high traffic area. 694-94 for those who know.<BR>I'm with the others and place a claim against their ins co. Find a couple of high end body shops and get some quotes. (We know it will just buff out, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> but it really should be buffed, blended, and resealed)<P>One little thing to keep in mind. How does your Ins co count accidents? If you live in a no fault state you may have points counted against you for just being there to be hit.||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||06-09-2001||05:37 AM||||Nail him. Beside the fact he probably does it often just him going to the cops and trying to report you makes it worth your while. Hit him for the damage and all associated court expenses if he trys to still be a smart ass SOB.<P>At least he will get a fine that way and a rise in his insurance premium.<P>Hey thats America isn't it. Can't you sue him for the emotional trauma too. Judge I can't go near my Fiero anymore, I get the shakes and have been having nightmares about being run over by a navigator. I am an emotional hertbroken mess judge sir. Can I have my million dollars now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000007||thomas_l||06-09-2001||08:00 AM||||I'd say pursue it! That guy was arrogant enough to not only hit you and drive away, but then LIE about it to the police! I'd get two high body repair estimates and sue his a$$.<P>About 10 years ago I had a run in with a similar liar back when I had my 78 Bonneville with no grill and primer paint  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. There is an on-ramp to I-75/85 in downtown Atlanta that I used to take going home. It starts two lanes wide, then narrows to one finally merging into a section that is 6 lanes wide. During rush hour, cars would squeeze through three abreast, with the right-most car travelling the breakdown lane. A **vulgar female anatomy reference goes here** in her nearly new Ford Probe decided to "squeeze" my lane. Traffic was moving about 5 mph and I was looking to move left 4 lanes to make my next exit, and was ignoring the Probe. I was 5 feet off the car in front and the nice lady drove right up into the bumper of my car. On mine, it scuffed the rub strip. She on the other hand had a nice inch-deep crease starting at her door all the way to the taillight.<P>In city court, she told the judge that I had appeared to let her merge then sped up and hit her. She had photos of her damage (after the fact) and two $1000 estimates. I told the judge I got scuffed and that my whole car wasn't even worth $100 so I didn't care about the damage I received. The judge threw it out as no-fault and told us to take care of our own cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> When we left the courtroom that woman was crying she was so mad! I grinned at her and said "tough luck b1tch". If looks could kill she would have mowed down 10 of me HAHAHAHAHA.||||reg||10
Z||000008||spideyfoot||06-09-2001||09:19 AM||||Sue the bas$$$$. Develop a severe neck pain. Come up with some weird stuff that could happen to a Fiero and charge him for it ( dogbone shifted, plastic stressed, possible implosion of gastank. Find out where he lives write yuppy prick on his lawn with gas. The thing that pisses me off is that he called the cops. ||||reg||1
